# C8 anion addition: find the H-bonded PS rotamer.
#
# The relaxed PS (ps_anion/job.xyz) is a minimum, but the O-O-H points at O130
# (the proximal peroxide O) instead of O129 (the alkoxide/carbonyl O):
#   H132...O129 = 3.845 A (no H-bond),  H132...O130 = 1.937 A,  angle 66 deg.
# That mis-conformation is why PS came out +129 kJ/mol above RS: the obvious
# intramolecular O-H...O- stabilisation is absent.
#
# Wanted: the five-membered O129-C128-O130-O131-H132 ring, with O129...H132 an
# H-bond. Scan the O-O-H torsion (C128-O130-O131-H132) a full turn to find that
# rotamer, then the best point is relaxed to a minimum.
#
# Seed = ps_anion/job.xyz (the mis-conformed minimum). Charge -1, 17-atom QM1.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) Opt TightOpt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132}
END
Charge_total -1
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  Scan
    D 128 130 131 132 = 0, 345, 24
  end
  MaxIter 200
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile -1 1 job.xyz
